Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 15:34:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Give generated Rust tests bounded default timeouts

Use short default timeouts for unit, binary-unit and integration test wrappers while preserving explicit crate overrides and None semantics. Keep verbose timeout diagnostics active. Analysis regressions reside beside private targets and retain platform compatibility restrictions.

Red: three real-target assertions expect short but observe moderate; long override controls pass. Green: all six analysis checks plus the actual ANSI unit suite pass with --platforms=//:rbe --extra_execution_platforms=//:rbe --test_verbose_timeout_warnings --test_output=errors. The full native platform suites remain acceptance gates. Fresh emitted verification includes just fmt-check and just bazel-lock-check.
